"""64-bit operands reading a 32-bit literal with bit 31 set, against words measured on RDNA2 (BUILD-713).

Every expected value was returned by the instructions themselves on an AMD Radeon RX 6900 XT (gfx1030, AMD driver
26.11.2, Windows) through tools/hw_oracle, single lane, wave32 and wave64 identical. A literal is sign-extended
when the operand is signed (s_ashr_i64, s_bfe_i64, s_flbit_i32_i64, v_ashrrev_i64, v_mad_i64_i32 src2,
v_cmp_*_i64) and zero-extended for every other 64-bit operand. Inline constants are sign-extended as before.
Each case leaves its result in v8..v11, which the translator exports here and the test compares word for word.

    python -m unittest discover -s tests/semantic -p "test_literal64_sign.py" -v
"""
